  "id": "dynamic-touch",
  "term": "dynamic touch",
  "definition": "Dynamic touch is the perception of properties of an object, such as its length, through active, forceful handling rather than by seeing it. In the source, it is studied by having a person wield an unseen object and judge it from the mechanical information available during movement.",
