      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims dynamic touch is perceived “rather than by seeing it,” but the packet only specifies the objects were “unseen” and does not explicitly contrast dynamic touch with vision in defining the term.",
        "The definition characterizes handling as “forceful”; while the packet mentions “forceful interaction with objects,” it does not state that dynamic touch is defined specifically as “active, forceful handling” in general (it discusses a particular task in children with ADHD).",
        "The packet supports that dynamic touch in this context involves length perception from information available during wielding, but it does not provide a general, 1–3 sentence conceptual definition matching the exact wording of the supplied definition (especially the explicit “rather than by seeing it” component)."
